~/psalms/129 {1 Many a time have they afflicted me from my youth, may Israel now say: / 2 Many a time have they afflicted me from my youth: yet they have not prevailed against me. / 3 The plowers plowed upon my back: they made long their furrows. / 4 The LORD is righteous: he hath cut asunder the cords of the wicked. / 5 Let them all be confounded and turned back that hate Zion. / 6 Let them be as the grass upon the housetops, which withereth afore it groweth up: / 7 Wherewith the mower filleth not his hand; nor he that bindeth sheaves his bosom. / 8 Neither do they which go by say, The blessing of the LORD be upon you: we bless you in the name of the LORD.}

